    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0327" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/87</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Havre</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Osborne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Havre</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Sjöstad</hi>, gross 1,755, Newport,
                    Wales, to Fécamp with coal, sunk 28th, noon, locality four or five minutes from
                    Cape Antifer, this district, either torpedoed or mined; 17 in crew; 9 missing
                    and believed drowned, comprising 4 Norwegians, 2 Swedes, 1 Finn, 1 Spaniard, 1
                    American named Smith, said to be from New York, aged about 25, shipped as
                    fireman, Newport, February 23. Ship’s papers lost. Eight survivors fell in sea;
                    rescued by French torpedo boats, which had convoyed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sjostad</hi>, and brought to Havre. Can not take depositions until 2d.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
